  "external_devices": {
    "pga": "proposed MCP6S21 at 3.3V; SPI CS/SCK/SI only, no SO; VSS and VREF to GND for unipolar stimulus; CH0 from same source tapped to A3; VOUT to A0. Gain write then verify measured A0/A3 ratio within unsaturated range; no register echo",
    "dac": "Proposed MCP4728 at 3.3V, 4 channels and I2C open-drain. TUL schematic sheet4 shows board R49/R50 nominal 2.2k pullups from AR_SCL/AR_SDA to VCC3V3; confirm fitted PCB and every module/adapter pullup before adding any external resistor; parallel equivalent is 1/(1/2200 + sum(1/Rmodule_i)) ohms. Microchip DS22187E section 7.1 describes typically 1-10k for standard/fast modes, with its Fig 7-1 showing 5-10k for 100-400kHz example; actual rise time and sink current depend on total bus capacitance. 7-bit address depends on EEPROM bits and actual module. DAC A feeds PGA CH0 and A3; B->A1; C->A2; D spare. J3 SCL/SDA physical contact numbers unresolved owing to manual/schematic conflict.",
    "rs485": "proposed TI THVD1450 at 3.3V half-duplex; D/RO/DE and active-low /RE connect to PL; transceiver A/B differential pair to PC-side RS485 adapter, common reference/termination/bias per cable topology; never wire A/B to PL GPIO"
  },
